&lt;p&gt;Faire is hiring a Senior Counsel, Regulatory &amp;amp; Product to advise the teams building our marketplace and to help us engage with the regulatory developments that shape it. This role is ideal for someone as excited about shaping the law as they are about advising on it. Reporting to the Deputy General Counsel, you&#39;ll partner closely with our product and engineering teams, helping them craft practical solutions to navigate legal complexity. You&#39;ll also build the muscle for identifying and tracking the legislative and regulatory developments that matter to Faire and to the brands and retailers on our platform. Working with stakeholders across the company and externally, you&#39;ll develop and advance positions to help the small businesses on our platform, and the local communities they anchor, thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with Faire’s engineering, product, data, and design teams to provide practical legal guidance across a wide range of legal domains on product development and go-to-market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor legislative and regulatory developments across local, state and federal jurisdictions and evaluate the potential implications for Faire and the small businesses that use our platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Faire&#39;s positions on potential legislation and regulation in partnership with stakeholders across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate emerging legal and regulatory obligations into practical product and operational requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with trade associations, coalitions, and external consultants to ensure cohesive advocacy efforts and alignment on priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Faire’s engagement and advocacy efforts with regulators, legislators, and their staff&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (JD) from an accredited law school and an active bar membership in at least one U.S. jurisdiction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience at a law firm, in-house, in government, and/or at a judicial clerkship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful exposure to how law and policy get made, either as a legislative aide, in an agency or administration, or through regulatory advocacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience counseling product teams and/or online marketplaces is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively experimenting with AI in legal work, and excited to go deeper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, including the ability to provide risk-calibrated and solution-focused advice to product and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappy and resourceful – when something needs to get done, you find a way to make it happen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
